title: Where am I?
new-page: true
go-to: two

You woke to your own screaming.

You look around, God, your head is pounding. 

You hear a noise, you turn, your friend, your *comrade* is staring at you. His white face paler still with shock. He stands up, suddenly, the ill fitting, rough suit hanging upon him. 

"!'4#$?" He cries out. You are panting heavily, he stands there, unsure what to do. "My ?5! are you alright?" He says, he is sweating, you are sweating. You nod, a lump in your throat, God you hate that lump. "Yes, Yes I'm fine, Axel."

Axel warmly smiles though his face is still in shock. "Right, you are fine then, 5@!~", my Comrade." You recoil a little from his proximity. I know, I know, you think, but the words don't come out. 

He stares at you. You realise you should speak. Your mouth opens, "ah- ba-" You close your mouth and try force the words out "Gah- uh- leh-" **FUCK!** You scream like a wolf. Axel takes a step back, he is scared. You hear him mutter, "The fuck-" under his breath

They always do this, every last one of them. It's aways something about YOU, never them. Never their own cowardice, never what they can't handle, it's always you, isn't it Adelyn? You breath heavily, you speak slowly, your nerves boiled, "I am...Fine." It takes you a few seconds to force it out.

Axel nods, he sits down on his chair, slowly, his knees bending. He is a young man, three years your Senior. His family were of the new middle class, emphasis upon the, were. Now their eldest son is sharing a room in Wedding with, well, you. You were never rich. You were kicked out at fifteen...

You try not to think about that.

You try think about the man in front of you.

